> Regarding the subject - How do I do that.

Always state your question in the message body.

As for your question, for floppy use

>>> boot dva0

and for CDROM use

>>> boot dka0

if your CDROM has SCSI id 0 on the first SCSI controller.  Otherwise
adjust the dka0 to something else.  The command "show dev" will list
all devices.

If you are wondering how to get to the SRM prompt, the answer is to
hit control-c at the right moment while booting, after the POST
countdown but before the boot process starts.

