From: Osmo Kujala (kujala@tukki.cc.jyu.fi)
 Subject: Adaptec 39160 (KZPEA) & OpenVMS ? 
 Newsgroups: comp.os.vms
 Date: 2002-10-11 00:45:02 PST 


Hi group!

Does anyone know, if it is possible to get Adaptec 39160 SCSI-card to
work with OpenVMS in EV5 Alpha? I know that KZPEA which has AIC-7899
chip like 39160 is supported on some EV6-models, but I've also seen
reports in Web that 39160 is working and regognized as KZPEA in
AlphaPC 164LX (EV5), with Tru64 at least.

Adaptec 29160 (AIC-7892) works in PWS 433a(u) with VMS 7.3 and 7.3-1
and in PC164 (Thanks to Patrick Young for valuable info!).
(Have to add entry in sys$user_config.dat if device Id is foreign.
7.3-1 has 7892 in sys$config.dat but the Device Id doesn't agree with
commodity 29160 card.)

For 39160 there is already right entry in sys$config.dat (right Device Id)
in 7.3-1 but the card doesn't work in PWS. Both channels of the card 
remain
offline and both have error count 1 . With 7.3 result was same but with
error counts of 3. (No I haven't yet analyzed those errors, thanks to that
stupid DECevent not installed.)

Should I wait that rest of the bugs get patches? Could the problem be with
bios emulation? I don't see anything about the card on monitor when I 
switch PWS on with SRM, but with Alphabios SCSIselect program of 39160
card is advertised and can be run.

Main difference between 7892 and 7899 chips (actually AIC-7892B and 
AIC-7899G) seems to be that 7899 is bigger and handles two channels.

Osmo



