modules.  Longevity-wise, it's too early to say.

While we're on the subject of UP2000 boards, does anyone have a 
definitive answer on jumper settings - J29 to be precise?  The UP2000+ 
manual gives a pinout for J29 which is totally at odds with the board 
silkscreen.  Even more curious, the manual mentions a jumper J31 for 
voltage setting.  The board I have is missing that completely, and has a 
voltage regulator w/ heatsink in that general area.

Although the manual claims that no jumpering is required (CPU sensing is 
claimed to be automagically done), the board will not POST unless I 
install a jumper on pins 11/12 of J29.  Depending upon who you believe, 
the manual claims this disables CPU Bcache - while the board silkscreen 
refers to that position as "TSUNAMI_SPEED1" and calls out 3/4 and 5/6 as 
Bcache disable for CPU 0 and 1 respectively.

